[
    {
        "content": "<p>Do we have that <code>minipoly</code> respects \"semilinear isomorphism\" of algebras? Like an <code>AlgEquiv</code> but it's across a <code>RingEquiv</code>, in the same way that a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LinearEquiv#doc\">docs#LinearEquiv</a> can be semilinear by changing the base ring with a <code>RingEquiv</code></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Ring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₁</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₁</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₂</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Ring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₂</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₂</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">eR</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃+*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">eS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃+*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">heRS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">algebraMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eR</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toRingHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eS</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toRingHom</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">algebraMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₁</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">minpoly</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eR</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">minpoly</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">eS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 613081618,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1785191054
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think it is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=minpoly.map_eq_of_equiv_equiv#doc\">docs#minpoly.map_eq_of_equiv_equiv</a> added in PR <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/27814\">#27814</a>. But I don't think it needs field and isomorphism as in its current statement. I think ring and injectivity suffices, just like <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=minpoly.algHom_eq#doc\">docs#minpoly.algHom_eq</a></p>",
        "id": 613114431,
        "sender_full_name": "Jz Pan",
        "timestamp": 1785211464
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is probably not true (or rather unprovable) because you run into issues when the minpoly is not uniquely specified. So you need to guarantee that somehow (e.g. integral elem of torsion-free over a domain, or something).</p>",
        "id": 613284850,
        "sender_full_name": "Albert Smith",
        "timestamp": 1785269363
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>minpoly.algHom_eq</code> can exist because you end up using choice on exactly the same predicate, no such luck here</p>",
        "id": 613285032,
        "sender_full_name": "Albert Smith",
        "timestamp": 1785269424
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>good thing my application is a field extension</p>",
        "id": 613287813,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1785270489
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>perhaps we can have this weaker statement?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Ring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₁</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₁</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₂</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Ring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₂</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₂</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">eR</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃+*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">eS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃+*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">heRS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">algebraMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eR</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toRingHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eS</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toRingHom</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">algebraMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₁</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">minpoly</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eR</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toRingHom</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">aeval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">eS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 613288637,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1785270751
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/.60minpoly.60.20respects.20isomorphism/near/613288637\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>perhaps we can have this weaker statement?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I think this should come from <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=minpoly.aeval#doc\">docs#minpoly.aeval</a> and that aeval commutes with map in some sense.</p>",
        "id": 613333495,
        "sender_full_name": "Jz Pan",
        "timestamp": 1785297481
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, it follows easily from what's in Mathlib (even for ring homs):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→+*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→+*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">algebraMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">algebraMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S₁</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">minpoly</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">aeval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Polynomial</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map_aeval_eq_aeval_map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 613543996,
        "sender_full_name": "Albert Smith",
        "timestamp": 1785371003
    }
